<Group labelreference="L7236" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">The exact solution for these parameters is <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>. We see that all stencils' output qualitatively resembles this decaying exponential for <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>. The backward Euler and trapezoidal stencils also capture the decay of the solution for <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> (though the trapezoidal results involve some suprious oscillations). However, forward Euler, Huen, and fourth order Runge-Kutta completely miss the basic shape of the exact solution; the numeric results appear to be exponentially growing in magnitude, not decaying. Since the absolute discrepancy between the exact and numerical result blows up as <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn</Equation> increases, we say that these stencils are unstable for <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> (in an absolute sense). We have the following definition.</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"><Font bold="true">Definition:</Font><Font bold="false"> A numerical stencil is said to be absolutely stable if the discrepancy between the numerical approximation and the exact solution does not grow exponentially as </Font><Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation><Font bold="false">.</Font></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">We can get a more systematic view of what is going on by plotting the global error (i.e., the absolute value of the difference between the exact and the numeric solutions) as a function of <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn</Equation> for various values of <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiekYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiekYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn</Equation>. The following procedure generates the data for this type of plot (with the errors reported as a logarithm).</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L7233" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">LogError := proc(lambda, z, X, choice)
    local data, N:
    data := Sol(lambda, abs(z/lambda), X, choice):
    N := nops(data):
    data := map(x -&gt; [x[1], log10(abs(x[2]-exp(lambda*x[1])))], data[2..N]):
    data := evalf(data):
end proc:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L7271" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Here are the plots of the global errors as a function of <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> We see that the two implicit stencils have global errors that are bounded as <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn</Equation> increases (i.e., stencils that are absolutely stable) for all <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> The three explicit stencils exhibit conditional stability in that for some <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiekYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiekYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn</Equation>, the errors grow exponentially while they remain bounded for other values of <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiekYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiekYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn</Equation>. For example, the forward Euler appears to be stable for <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> and unstable for <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
