<Group labelreference="L7283" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Now, the reader may be wondering what the practical import of this discussion is. While the explicit stencils have stability issues when <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> is large and <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>, one can always obtain stable results when the stepsize is small enough. In other words, the explicit stencils will work as long as we are willing to wait long enough for results. However, the situation is a lot different if we consider imaginary <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEnJiM5NTU7RicvJSdpdGFsaWNHUSZmYWxzZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdGMS8lLG1hdGh2YXJpYW50R1Enbm9ybWFsRidGMkY0">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEnJiM5NTU7RicvJSdpdGFsaWNHUSZmYWxzZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdGMS8lLG1hdGh2YXJpYW50R1Enbm9ybWFsRidGMkY0</Equation>. When <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> is complex, both the analytic solution <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> and the numeric solution will be complex, and hence difficult to plot. So, in the plots below, we will plot the real part of the numerical solutions, which ought to be an approximation to <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>, where <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>. The <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">plotter2</Font> procedure accomplishes this.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L7270" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">plotter2 := (lambda, h, X, choice) -&gt; plot([map(x -&gt; [x[1], Re(x[2])], Sol(lambda, h, X, choice)), Re(exp(lambda*x))], x = 0..X, axes = boxed, title = typeset(Labels[choice], ` with `, z = lambda*h, ` (real part of solution)`), legend = [`numeric solution`, typeset(Re(exp(lambda*x)))]):</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L7253" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Here are some plots of the output of the forward Euler stencil when <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEnJiM5NTU7RicvJSdpdGFsaWNHUSZmYWxzZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdGMS8lLG1hdGh2YXJpYW50R1Enbm9ybWFsRidGMkY0">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEnJiM5NTU7RicvJSdpdGFsaWNHUSZmYWxzZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdGMS8lLG1hdGh2YXJpYW50R1Enbm9ybWFsRidGMkY0</Equation> is imaginary. In each plot, the numeric results appear to diverge from the expected analytic result for large <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn</Equation> irrespective of the choice of stepsize (or, conversely, irrespective of the modulus of <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiekYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiekYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn</Equation>). We say that the forward Euler stencil is unconditionally unstable when <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEnJiM5NTU7RicvJSdpdGFsaWNHUSZmYWxzZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdGMS8lLG1hdGh2YXJpYW50R1Enbm9ybWFsRidGMkY0">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEnJiM5NTU7RicvJSdpdGFsaWNHUSZmYWxzZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdGMS8lLG1hdGh2YXJpYW50R1Enbm9ybWFsRidGMkY0</Equation> is imaginary.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
