<Group labelreference="L7300" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">We would now like to attempt to explain some of the behaviour witnessed in the previous section. We will need to have expressions for each of the above stencils that include the one-step error, which we call <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">_Stencil</Font>. These are generated by the following code.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L7291" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">derivative[1] := D(y)(x) = f(x, y(x)):
for j from 2 to 5 do:
    derivative[j] := subs(derivative[1], convert(diff(derivative[j-1], x), D)):
od:

Subs := [y_new = y(x+h), y_old = y(x), x_new = x+h, x_old = x]:

for j from 1 to 5 do:
    one_step[j] := O(h^ldegree(convert(simplify(subs(convert(derivative, list), series(subs(Subs, lhs(Stencil[j])), h))), polynom), h)):
    _Stencil[j] := subs(Subs, lhs(Stencil[j])) = one_step[j]:
    print(Labels[j], _Stencil[j]):
od:</Text-field>
</Input>
