<Group labelreference="L7308" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">In these plots, the red region shows where each stencil is stable. The shapes of the stability regions explain many of the features seen in the previous section: for example, it is clear that the forward Euler stencil is stable on the real axis for <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> and unstable for all finite <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiekYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiekYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn</Equation> on the imaginary axis. It is interesting to actually plot <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> for imaginary <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiekYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiekYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn</Equation> for the RK4 stencil:</Text-field>
